    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "node-eol",
      "lines": [
        "engines.node ^23.0.0 in package.json admits only end-of-life Node lines: the release is built on Node 23, which reached end of life on 2025-06-01.",
        "  That Node receives no security fixes, and the lockfile is resolved for it. The oldest line still maintained is Node 22.",
        "  Node release dates from schedule.json of nodejs/Release, as of 2026-11-13."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "warn",
      "id": "license-drift",
      "lines": [
        "Licence AGPL (appinfo/info.xml), AGPLv3 (package.json).",
        "  AGPL in appinfo/info.xml is a deprecated App Store value, shown there as AGPLv3+, which is AGPL-3.0-or-later. An SPDX id there needs a <nextcloud> min-version of 31 or higher.",
        "  No SPDX id: AGPLv3 (package.json). Only an SPDX id says which licence is meant, and for a GNU licence whether -only or -or-later.",
        "  No LICENSES/ directory, so the licence text itself is not in the checkout, which is what REUSE and the distributions check for."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "app-id",
      "lines": [
        "The app id is switchboardbridge, the checkout directory is B2Drop2LRS.",
        "  The server finds an app by its directory name, so the installed directory has to be named after the id. A checkout can be named anything, which is why this is a note and not a defect - but a tarball built from this directory name would not load."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "link-redirect",
      "lines": [
        "A link of appinfo/info.xml has moved permanently:",
        "  <bugs> https://github.com/clarin-eric/B2Drop2LRSwitchboard/issues",
        "    now https://github.com/clarin-eric/B2Drop2LRS/issues",
        "  The old address works only as long as the redirect is kept; the new one can be stated directly."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "nextcloud-support",
      "lines": [
        "Declares Nextcloud 28 to 35; the oldest maintained major is 33 (the Maintenance and Release Schedule of nextcloud/server), the newest released 35 (the release tags of nextcloud/server).",
        "  min-version 28 reaches below the oldest maintained major (33), which means the code has to keep working with APIs that are no longer tested upstream."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "node-version",
      "lines": [
        "Node stated as ^23.0.0 (package.json engines.node), 23.x (main.yml).",
        "  Not stated in .nvmrc, so nothing keeps the other places from drifting away from it.",
        "  The checks run on another Node: 22.x (main.yml). They lint and test the code and build no release asset, so this decides only what those runs see."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "tooling",
      "lines": [
        "Tooling in the checkout: ESLint (eslint.config.mjs).",
        " No Stylelint configuration: stylesheets are unchecked, and a mistake in CSS fails silently instead of loudly.",
        " No Psalm configuration: the PHP side has no static analysis, which is what catches a wrong type before the server does.",
        " No PHPUnit configuration: there is no test harness in the checkout, so nothing can be run against a change.",
        " No PHP-CS-Fixer configuration: no coding standard is applied to the PHP sources, so formatting is settled in review instead of by a command.",
        " No REUSE configuration: licensing is not machine-checkable, which the App Store and every distribution ask for.",
        " No EditorConfig configuration: indentation is whatever each contributor's editor does."
      ]
    },
    {
      "level": "info",
      "id": "unreferenced-dependencies",
      "lines": [
        "3 declared packages are named nowhere in the checkout: @eslint/eslintrc, @eslint/js, eslint-import-resolver-custom-alias.",
        "  Searched as literal names over 124 files, package.json excluded apart from its non-dependency fields, lockfiles excluded; then as an ESLint shorthand, as what TypeScript takes from a tsconfig, and as a peer of an installed package in package-lock.json. A package loaded some other way is not named anywhere either, so this is a list to check, not a list to remove."
      ]
    },
